      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-11658",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/87/875f3f1689e8c6fe1dd4887f5c1e5855d1cdc7e9eb8800ac2a4384fce4de2aa1.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed by the curve $x = 5(y^{2} - y^{3}) - 1$ and the line $x =-1$. Cross-sections perpendicular to the $y$-axis are rectangles. Given that the height of each rectangle is $\\frac{1}{25}$ times the length of its base, calculate the volume of the solid.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
