      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-50429",
      ":question/problem": "The base of a solid is the region enclosed by the curve $x =-2y + y^{2} + 1$ and the line $x = 1$. Cross-sections perpendicular to the $y$-axis are rectangles. If the height of each rectangle is $2$ times the length of its base, which integral gives the volume of the solid?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
